WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.111
Step 1. Open the charge item definitions.

1.2
00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:08.484
A charge item definition is the reusable price of a service or item that your

1.3
00:00:08.484 --> 00:00:14.218
facility bills. In Settings, under Billing, select Charge Item Definitions.

2.1
00:00:14.218 --> 00:00:16.306
Step 2. Open the category.

2.2
00:00:16.306 --> 00:00:20.407
Open categories until you reach one with no subcategories,

2.3
00:00:20.407 --> 00:00:26.210
then select Add Definition. Care shows this button only in such a category.

3.1
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:31.794
Step 3. Enter the basic details. Enter the Title, and Care fills in the Slug.

3.2
00:00:31.794 --> 00:00:37.628
The Category is the one that you opened, and the Status is Active by default.

4.1
00:00:37.628 --> 00:00:41.608
Step 4. Enter the additional details. These are optional.

4.2
00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:46.844
Keep Can Edit Charge Item selected to let staff change the price and quantity of

4.3
00:00:46.844 --> 00:00:49.569
charge items from this definition.

5.1
00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:51.634
Step 5. Enter the prices.

5.2
00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:56.354
Base Price is the standard price of one unit, and it is required.

5.3
00:00:56.354 --> 00:01:02.373
MRP and Purchase Price are kept for information and do not change the total.

6.1
00:01:02.373 --> 00:01:06.399
Step 6. Add taxes. Under Taxes, select Add tax.

6.2
00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:10.094
Select the check box of each tax that applies.

6.3
00:01:10.094 --> 00:01:15.976
If a tax code has more than one rate, select one, then select Done.

7.1
00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:21.570
Step 7. Add discounts. Select Add Discount and choose the discounts that apply.

7.2
00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:26.915
For each one, use the facility global value, or override it with a local value,

7.3
00:01:26.915 --> 00:01:29.174
which can have conditions.

8.1
00:01:29.174 --> 00:01:31.272
Step 8. Save the definition.

8.2
00:01:31.272 --> 00:01:35.365
Check the base price in the Price Summary, then select Create.

8.3
00:01:35.365 --> 00:01:41.015
Care shows Charge item definition created successfully and opens the category.
